# POA v2: Proof of Attendance

> Privacy-preserving attendance tracking using Zero-Knowledge Location Proofs (ZKLP)

## Overview

POA v2 is a complete rewrite of the original Ethereum-based attendance system, now built on the **Aztec Network** using the **ZKLP (Zero-Knowledge Location Proofs)** protocol.

### Why ZKLP?

The original Ethereum implementation exposed all data publicly:
- Wallet addresses
- Check-in/check-out timestamps
- Location history
- Employer-employee relationships

**ZKLP solves this** by enabling privacy-preserving proof of presence:
- **Anonymous**: Smart lock doesn't know who's accessing
- **Non-transferable**: Credentials bound to identity
- **Verifiable**: Managers can audit via encrypted records
- **Secure**: Nullifiers prevent replay attacks

## Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                     POA v2 SYSTEM                           │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                             │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │  ZKLP Protocol (aztec-zklp-protocol)                │   │
│  │  ├── generate_zklp()                                │   │
│  │  ├── verify_zklp()                                  │   │
│  │  ├── Identity management                            │   │
│  │  └── Nullifier-based sessions                       │   │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                          ▲                                  │
│                          │ Uses                              │
│                          ▼                                  │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │  POA Attendance (this repo)                         │   │
│  │  ├── Organization management                        │   │
│  │  ├── Unit (location) registry                       │   │
│  │  ├── Employee management                            │   │
│  │  ├── Check-in/out operations                        │   │
│  │  └── Manager dashboard                              │   │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                                                             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- [Aztec Sandbox](https://docs.aztec.network/developers/getting-started)
- Node.js 18+

### Installation

```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/[user]/poa-attendance.git
cd poa-attendance

# Install dependencies
cd aztec-js
npm install

# Build
npm run build
```

### Usage

```typescript
import { POAClient, EmployeeClient, Role } from '@poa/attendance';
import { createIdentity } from '@poa/zklp-protocol';

// Setup
const poaClient = new POAClient(pxe, wallet, contractAddress);

// Manager creates organization
const orgId = await poaClient.createOrganization(
  Fr.fromString("My Company"),
  ownerAddress,
  Fr.ZERO
);

// Manager registers unit
const unitId = await poaClient.registerUnit(
  orgId,
  Fr.fromString("Office A"),
  locationHash,
  credentialRoot
);

// Manager registers employee
const employeeIdentity = createIdentity(masterSecret);
await poaClient.registerEmployee(
  employeeIdentity,
  orgId,
  Role.Staff,
  [unitId]
);

// Employee checks in
const employeeClient = new EmployeeClient(poaClient, masterSecret);
const { zklp, session } = await employeeClient.checkIn(unitId, merkleProof);

// Smart lock verifies
const valid = await poaClient.verifyCheckIn(zklp, viewingKey);
if (valid) {
  // Open door
}

// Employee checks out
const { zklp: exitZKLP } = await employeeClient.checkOut(
  unitId,
  zklp.nullifier,
  merkleProof
);
```

## Repository Structure

```
poa-attendance/
├── contracts/              # Noir smart contracts
│   ├── Nargo.toml         # Contract dependencies (uses zklp_protocol)
│   └── main.nr            # POAAttendance contract
├── aztec-js/              # TypeScript SDK
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── index.ts       # Main exports
│   │   ├── types.ts       # POA-specific types
│   │   └── poa.ts         # POAClient, EmployeeClient, ManagerClient
│   └── package.json
├── smart-lock/            # Smart lock verifier
├── manager-dashboard/     # Web dashboard for managers
├── tests/                 # Test suite
│   ├── unit/
│   └── e2e/
└── AZTEC_MIGRATION.md     # Migration documentation
```

## Key Features

### For Employees
- **Private check-in/out**: Identity hidden from smart lock
- **Mobile app**: Generate ZKLPs on-device
- **Session tracking**: Automatic check-out reminders

### For Managers
- **Organization management**: Create orgs, units, manage employees
- **Audit trail**: Encrypted records viewable with viewing key
- **Payroll integration**: Export hours worked

### For Smart Locks
- **Zero-knowledge verification**: Verify without learning identity
- **Offline capable**: Cache credential roots
- **Tamper-proof**: Cryptographic verification

## Privacy Model

| Data | Smart Lock | Blockchain | Manager |
|------|-----------|------------|---------|
| Employee Identity | ❌ Hidden | ❌ Hidden | ✅ Visible |
| Location | ✅ Known | ❌ Hidden | ✅ Visible |
| Timestamp | ✅ Known | ❌ Hidden | ✅ Visible |
| Work History | ❌ Hidden | ❌ Hidden | ✅ Visible |

